        <mxCell id="legend" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F5F5F5;strokeColor=none;fontSize=10;align=left;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;verticalAlign=top;" value="&lt;b&gt;Reading this diagram&lt;/b&gt; &amp;nbsp; Solid arrows are the run. Dashed grey arrows are reads and writes. Red is the escalation path.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;No stage holds both Terraform state access and a repository write credential&lt;/b&gt; — which is why gates is a separate stage from codify.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;① detect&lt;/b&gt; &amp;nbsp; Reads state; no GitHub credential. Intersects a refresh-only plan with a full plan — refresh-only alone reports provider normalization as drift.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;② codify&lt;/b&gt; &amp;nbsp; GitHub App token and Bedrock; state access denied outright. Verifies its own diff against the authorized change before publishing.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;③ gates&lt;/b&gt; &amp;nbsp; Reads state and live resources; no GitHub credential. Gate B: Checkov on the branch plan. Gate C: Checkov on source, because a plan is blind to ignore_changes. Both verdicts are deltas against a baseline.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;④ finalize&lt;/b&gt; &amp;nbsp; The codify project under a buildspec override, so the credential that opened the PR is the one that labels it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The PR opens as &lt;b&gt;do-not-merge&lt;/b&gt; + &lt;b&gt;gates-pending&lt;/b&gt;, flips to &lt;b&gt;drift-codified&lt;/b&gt; on pass, and waits for review. App token: one repository, one hour." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="1240" x="40" y="700" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
